      ],
      "status": "closed",
      "bucket": "A",
      "scope_notes": "All four steps, for the loop closure and the truncation at once via the cap parameter; the paper's `d < m <= K/2` is hdm plus hD : HasDouble cap m, and evenness of K is unused. eq:doubling_step3 is stated SQUARED (Stat.mass is the p-th power of the norm), equivalent to the paper's square-root form. Stat.mass_centredTail is proved with NO hypothesis on p (the paper assumes p in [1,inf)): f_m takes two values, so the identity is exact at every exponent. The identity of Step 2 is asserted OnChain and genuinely fails at lad(K+1), where lambda vanishes."
    },
